%% Login with a single sign-on provider: Authorization Code Flow with PKCE (src/sso.py, Authlib)
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User
    participant Browser
    participant Frontend
    participant Provider as OIDC provider
    participant Database as PostgreSQL

    User->>Browser: clicks the button of the provider
    Browser->>Frontend: GET /login/sso/alias
    Frontend->>Provider: discovery document (timeout 5 s + 10 s)
    Frontend-->>Browser: redirect to the provider<br>state, nonce, PKCE challenge kept in the session
    Browser->>Provider: the user logs in
    Provider-->>Browser: redirect to /login/sso/alias/callback?code&state
    Browser->>Frontend: GET callback
    Frontend->>Provider: exchange the code (PKCE verifier, client secret)
    Provider-->>Frontend: ID token
    Frontend->>Frontend: check state, nonce, signature, issuer, audience, expiration
    Frontend->>Database: find the identity by issuer and subject
    alt identity found
        Database-->>Frontend: user
    else verified or trusted email of an existing user (never an administrator)
        Frontend->>Database: link the identity to that user
    else the provider creates accounts
        Frontend->>Database: create the user and its identity
    else
        Frontend-->>Browser: login rejected
    end
    Frontend->>Frontend: new session, log login
    Frontend-->>Browser: redirect to the next page (safe_next_url)
